[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Verification audit remediation criteria

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Independently justified expected behavior
STATEMENT: Compatibility evidence shall identify whether each expected behavior comes from the specification, an independently checked mathematical contract, a pinned implementation observation, or an intentionally reproduced implementation quirk.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Complete result observations
STATEMENT: Quantity differential observations shall jointly retain returned value, numeric representation mapping, scale and unit identity, and distinguish expected failure stage and approved exception mappings. Each component shall have a negative witness demonstrating detection of independent corruption.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Strict comparison and fixture schemas
STATEMENT: Verification tools shall reject malformed or contradictory outcomes, duplicate or missing case identifiers, empty qualification inventories and nonfinite or unapproved tolerances; compare exact integers without binary64 loss; and require explicit per-case tolerances for approximate comparisons.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Assertion-specific closure evidence
STATEMENT: A verified assertion shall resolve its pinned source occurrence, corresponding API surface and executable semantic tests, tested revision, Java provenance, required platform CI evidence and reviewer decision; inventory accounting shall be distinguished from evidence qualification.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Mutation qualification scope and provenance
STATEMENT: Mutation reports shall identify tested source and test revisions, distinguish historical from final-source campaigns, disposition survivors and uncovered mutants, and demonstrate that critical historical semantic faults are detected without counting ignored or uncompiled mutants as verified behavior.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. The2026-10-30 debt reduction, targeted public boundaries, promotion correction, Java chain evidence and reviewed survivor dispositions are retained in conformance/mutation-debt.md and its manifests. Raw mutation outcomes are preserved; equivalent or out-of-contract classifications are not kills or formal TCK closure.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Independent review and honest qualification verdict
STATEMENT: A verification audit shall retain an independent reviewer assessment, findings and dispositions, explicitly identify agent versus human review, and qualify completion claims according to unresolved evidence gaps rather than aggregate test counts.
COMMENT: Accepted audit repair criterion. Implementation and executable test/evidence mapping: conformance/verification-repair.md and conformance/verification-repair-results.json. Active is a requirements lifecycle state, not formal TCK verification. All actual assertion closures remain gated on attested Windows/Ubuntu/Java execution and review.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-HASH-QUALITY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded converter hash-quality robustness criterion
STATEMENT: A seeded engineering workload of32 structurally distinct converters shall retain at least8 distinct hash buckets across100 recorded FsCheck trials, permitting ordinary collisions and retaining generated inputs and dictionary equality-comparison counts.
COMMENT: Inferred engineering acceptance choice for catastrophic constant hashing, not a JSR conformance rule, exact hash-value contract, general distribution proof or benchmark claim. Seed385,905. Implementation verification: MutationDebtHashQualityTests; evidence: conformance/mutation-debt-hash-quality.json and mutation-debt.md. Raw mutation survival retains its functional equality/hash-contract distinction.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: VER-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-RAILWAY-ERRORS
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Actionable typed numeric boundary failures
STATEMENT: Additive numeric parsing and conversion boundaries shall return either a non-null value or a typed expected failure with a stable error code and input parameter, including a character offset when known. Composition shall forward failure without invoking downstream work. Existing throwing APIs shall preserve exception types and parameter names. Unexpected faults and cancellation shall not be converted into expected failures.
COMMENT: User-approved design 2026-11-12 in docs/typed-error-survivors-design.md. Implementation: src/SharpUnits/NumericResult.cs and JavaNumber.ParseDecimal/ConvertNumeric; verification: TypedNumericResultTests, seeded replays385,1101 and385,1103, and conformance/typed-errors.md. Exact diagnostic wording is separate from stable error identity. Active denotes the accepted requirement lifecycle, not a formal TCK closure. This is a CLR usability requirement, not Java API equivalence.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: VER-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-SURVIVOR-REPLAY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Survivor remediation measured on changed source
STATEMENT: Survivor remediation shall retain source-bound mutation outcomes, targeted negative witnesses and line and branch coverage for changed code. Revised or removed source statements shall not be counted as killed mutants. Equivalent mutations, observable variations outside the accepted contract, uncovered statements and inconclusive timeouts shall retain separate dispositions.
COMMENT: User-requested survivor follow-up. Historical outcomes remain in conformance/mutation-debt-reviewed.json. New evidence is retained separately in conformance/typed-errors.md and typed-errors-mutations.json. Error-code mutations challenge actionable typed contracts rather than English wording. No global mutation-score improvement or formal closure is inferred from a changed mutant universe.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: VER-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VER-RUN-BUDGET
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Guarded Windows verification admission and commit budgets
STATEMENT: The Windows verification wrapper shall refuse concurrent same-user guarded workloads, confirm requested process and aggregate job commit limits by native read-back before releasing work, retain limits and observed peaks, and terminate owned descendants on a recorded limit event or fail-fast watermark even when the root has exited successfully.
COMMENT: User resource-budget policy applied to local verification. Implementation: tools/Invoke-Budgeted.ps1 and Invoke-TypedErrorVerification.ps1. Tests: Test-BudgetWatchdog.ps1, including root-exits-zero, and Test-BudgetAdmission.ps1. An85-percent watermark with250ms peak reconciliation supplements Windows best-effort limit notifications. These are commit limits, not RSS limits or a reservation against other applications; Linux cgroup execution and exhaustive crash/race qualification are outside this Windows helper. See conformance/typed-errors.md for failed initial flag assignment, correction, actual read-back and replay evidence.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: VER-005
